  "pdf_bytes": 859322,
  "selection": "Curated. The first three, in order, of the four prompts of the previous fig:qual_main (fig_qual_main.PROMPTS), which were picked by hand for variety from the 191 evaluation prompts (fig_qual.py MAIN, kept by the 2026-10-18 redesign). The fourth, the ivy archway m1057810871814672649, is left out for space. History: a first draft dropped the portrait m2729538226706404616 instead, because its crops differed least between methods, a choice made before any per-image value was read. Its values, read afterwards, made it the one prompt of the four where SCA does not have the best MUSIQ_c (HRDiT does), so that visual criterion favoured SCA. It was replaced by the order rule, which looks at neither the images nor the values. No metric ranked the prompts. All six fig_qual.py MAIN prompts are excluded from the uncurated galleries.",
  "crop_rule": "Automatic, not hand-placed: fig_qual_main.auto_box over full, area, hrdit and sca, i.e. the 320x240 (width x height) window with the largest mean PIL FIND_EDGES response of the 8x box-downsampled greyscale images, at least 256 px from every border. The same window is cropped from every method; layouts differ between methods, so the crops differ in content.",
  "metric": "MUSIQ_c (CSV column musiq_crop1024): pyiqa MUSIQ averaged over four fixed random 1024^2 crops per image, crop positions set by the prompt id and shared across methods (Appendix app:metrics). It is a per-image score, not a score of the displayed window. Printed to one decimal; the best printed value per row is bold.",
